SUMMARY:🟩 CE 311S · Lab · #17650 · 4–5pm
LOCATION:ECJ 2.218
DESCRIPTION:DELETE this whole series if your unique number is not 17650.\
 nIn Outlook\, open any one of these and choose Delete series.\nMonday 4
 –5pm\, ECJ 2.218. TA Sadab Khan\, sk67837@my.utexas.edu.\nThe all-day e
 vent on each Monday names that week's lab or review.\nThe lecture syllabu
 s lists unique numbers 17645\, 17650\, 17655\, and 17660. The lab syllabu
 s pairs 17645\, 17655\, 17660\, and 17650 with 1–2\, 2–3\, 3–4\, an
 d 4–5. Confirm your registration.\nAttendance is mandatory. Email befor
 e lab if you will miss it\, or that lab is a zero.\nNo lab is dropped. La
 bs are 5% of the grade.\nBring a laptop and a printed lab report. Excel i
 s required. One hard-copy report per pair.\nThe lab syllabus says finish 
 during the 50 minutes or turn the report in by midnight that Monday. The 
 lecture syllabus says within 7 days. Use midnight unless the TA says othe
 rwise.\nOverlaps the first hour of EM 306 discussion #16220 (Mon 4:00–6
 :00 pm).\n\nAug 24: Lab 0 — Calculus review.\nAug 31: Lab 1 — Probabi
 lity in lifeline design.\nSep 14: Review — Exam 1 review.\nSep 21: Lab 
 2 — Waste containment probabilities.\nSep 28: Lab 3 — Construction la
 bor costs.\nOct 5: Review — Exam 2 review.\nOct 12: Lab 4 — Levee des
 ign\, normal distribution.\nOct 19: Lab 5 — Hydraulic conductivity\, lo
 gnormal.\nOct 26: Lab 6 — Column reliability.\nNov 2: Review — Exam 3
  review.\nNov 9: Lab 7 — Mercury emission intervals.\nNov 16: Review 
 — Exam 4 review.\nNov 30: Lab 8 — Income regression.\nDec 7: Review 
 — Final exam review.
