SUMMARY:🟧 CE 311K · Lecture · MATLAB and numerical methods
LOCATION:RLP 0.102
DESCRIPTION:CE 311K Introduction to Computer Methods.\nTuesday and Thursd
 ay\, 8:00–9:30 am\, RLP 0.102.\nThe syllabus has a topic outline\, not 
 a day-by-day schedule:\n1. Introduction to computing\, simulations\, oper
 ating systems\, round-off and truncation error.\n2. MATLAB: environment\,
  structured programming\, arrays\, control flow\, scripts and functions\,
  graphing\, symbolic operations.\n3. Numerical methods: error\, roots\, c
 urve fitting\, integration and differentiation\, Ax = b\, ODEs\, finite d
 ifferences.\nInstructor: Dr. Othman Oudghiri-Idrissi\, ECJ 4.706\, othman
 oi@utexas.edu.\nHomework and lab due dates are not listed. They are due a
 t 11:59 pm on the Canvas date. You have three penalty-free late days tota
 l.\nAttendance at lecture and lab is mandatory.\nOctober 13 and November 
 19 are exams\, so this repeating lecture skips those mornings.
